rtnerships (project-level funding reported).\",\"url\":\"https://www.subnational.finance/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/global-assessment-of-recycling-technologies-for-low-value-plastic-waste.pdf\"},{\"name\":\"Sierra Energy\",\"why_similar\":\"Thermal conversion of municipal solid waste to energy/fuels with commercial demonstration facilities—competes in waste-to-energy/fuels space.\",\"funding\":\"Has institutional partnerships and project funding for demonstration plants.\",\"url\":\"https://www.closedlooppartners.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/CLP_Molecular-Recycling-Directory-2021.pdf\"},{\"name\":\"WasteFuel (formerly Renewlogy/WasteFuel)\",\"why_similar\":\"Converts waste into fuels and chemicals; listed among funded waste-to-fuels companies.\",\"funding\":\"Listed with institutional funding (Dealroom summary reports ~USD millions).\",\"url\":\"https://dealroom.co/lists/waste-to-energy-startups/\"}]","series_a_risk":"high","series_a_notes":"Positives: TUM PhD origin and named technical founders are credible for hard-science diligence (user-provided); Breakthrough Energy Fellows selection is a strong external validation signal (user-provided). Risks: no IP found in web checks, crowded market flagged with Enerkem, Brightmark, Licella/Cat-HTR, Sierra Energy and WasteFuel as comparables, and the company is described as moving from lab to commercial scale, which is usually pre-bankability (model judgement). Series A survivability depends on showing protected process know-how or filed IP, continuous pilot data on real hard-to-recycle waste, credible unit economics, and signed feedstock/offtake partners before raising (model judgement).","grant_bridges":"[{\"programme\":\"EIC Accelerator\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits high-risk, high-impact climate deep-tech with scale-up needs; useful if Valoron can show a breakthrough process, EU impact and a credible commercialisation plan.\",\"source\":\"https://eic.ec.europa.eu/eic-funding-opportunities/eic-accelerator_en\"},{\"programme