ded in industry/NIH resource lists of suppliers.\",\"funding\":\"commercial supplier\",\"url\":\"https://commonfund.nih.gov/Glycoscience/otherresources\"}]","series_a_risk":"medium","series_a_notes":"User-provided signals are positive: team score 90, fit 79, low flight risk, founder-owned IP and a pilot-customer quote on price/quality/delivery. Model judgement: survivability is better than therapeutic biotech because revenue can start early, but Series A risk remains medium due to niche glycobiology market, medium crowding from established reagent suppliers, and the need to prove scalable GMP-ready manufacturing plus a differentiated glyco-plug-in platform.","grant_bridges":"[{\"programme\":\"EIC Accelerator\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits if eversyn can frame the glyco-plug-in as a high-risk, high-impact European biomanufacturing platform with strong commercial pull beyond reagent sales.\",\"source\":\"https://eic.ec.europa.eu/eic-funding-opportunities/eic-accelerator_en\"},{\"programme\":\"SPRIND\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits only if the platform is positioned as a disruptive leap in precision glycosylation or distributed glycan manufacturing; less suitable for ordinary reagent scale-up.\",\"source\":\"https://www.sprind.org/en/\"},{\"programme\":\"BMBF KMU-innovativ: Biomedicine / Biotechnology\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits SME R&D on enzymatic synthesis, process development, analytics and biomanufacturing applications for pharma or nutrition customers.\",\"source\":\"https://www.bmbf.de/bmbf/de/forschung/gesundheit/gesundheitswirtschaft/kmu-innovativ/kmu-innovativ_node.html\"},{\"programme\":\"EXIST-Forschungstransfer\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits if eversyn is still eligible as a university/research spin-out and needs to de-risk transfer from academic IP into scalable products; eligibility must be checked because the GmbH is already founded.\",\"source\":\"https://www.exist.de/EXIST/Navigation/DE/Gruendungsfoerderung/EXIST-Forschungstransfer/exist-forschungstransfer.html\"},{\"programme\":\"Eurostars\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits collaborative R&D with European biopharma, nutrition or enzyme-technology partners where eversyn is the SME commercial lead for glycosylation workflows.\",\"source\":\"https://www.eurekanetwork.org/programmes/eurostars/\"},{\"programme\":\"ZIM - Zentrales Innovationsprogramm Mittelstand\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits applied SME R&D and cooperation projects for process scale-up, custom manufacturing workflows and productisation of nucleotide-sugar synthesis.\",\"source\":\"https://www.zim.de/ZIM/Navigation/DE/Home/home.html\"}]","intro_path":"Intro via cutanos (also from Max Planck Institute of Colloids; https://www.htgf.de/en/portfolio/htgffamily/cutanos/)","commitment":null,"bus_factor":null,"domain_age_days":1691,"deep_signals":"{\"evidence_hash\":\"qrp29a\",\"checked_at\":\"2026-11-20T23:04:24.229Z\",\"rank\":1,\"flight_code_signals\":[\"English-only website\"],\"flight_web\":[{\"claim\":\"Company website states solutions, customers and 'Backed by' German organisations (bmp Ventures, Max Planck Foundation, EXIST) and lists Magdeburg presence; company presents as a Max Planck spin-off.\",\"url\":\"https://www.eversyn.de/\"},{\"claim\":\"Commercial register entry shows eversyn GmbH registered at HRB 33897 (Amtsgericht Stendal) with an address in Halle/Magdeburg region (Germany).\",\"url\":\"https://handelsregister.ai/en/organizations/halle-saale/research-and-experimental-development-on-biotechnology/eversyn-gmbh-c7a16da41d66b7a3ae2db3015b509083\"}],\"funding_found\":{\"claim\":\"Seed round of €1.6 million led by bmp ventures with co-investments from Max Planck Society/MPF Start-Up Accelerator and a strategic business angel (closed seed financing).\",\"url\":\"https://www.max-planck-innovation.com/max-planck-innovation/news/press-releases/press-release/max-planck-spin-off-eversyn-secures-1-6-million-in-seed-funding.html\"},\"hq_outside_germany\":null,\"ip\":[{\"claim\":\"Company website lists 'Patent assets' and claims 5 patent