ore_version":2,"scored_at":"2026-11-20T22:53:45.437Z","priority":361,"website":"https://vasc-on-demand.eu","news_status":"checked: 13 result(s), first public mention found","deep_checked_at":"2026-11-20T23:04:24.229Z","flight_risk":"low","flight_risk_evidence":"[{\"claim\":\"English-only website\",\"url\":\"website text (flow 14)\"},{\"claim\":\"Project and team repeatedly presented as Würzburg / Universitätsklinikum Würzburg; no evidence of US accelerator participation or a US legal entity.\",\"url\":\"https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/101156395/results\"},{\"claim\":\"Würzburg-based project coverage and local awards (Innovation Award, IGZ support) — indicates Germany-based activities.\",\"url\":\"https://www.bio-m.org/en/media-center/news/news/nnovationspreis-der-bioregionen-deutschlands-2026-wuerzburger-projekt-vasc-on-demand-unter-den-preistraegern\"}]","ip_status":"university_owned","ip_evidence":"[{\"claim\":\"Patent application listed for the project: 'DEVICE FOR FABRICATING A PERFUSABLE THREE-DIMENSIONAL TISSUE CONSTRUCT' — applicant: UNIVERSITAETSKLINIKUM WUERZBURG - KLINIKUM DER BAYERISCHEN JULIUS-MAXIMILIANS-UNIVERSITAT.\",\"url\":\"https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/101156395/results\"},{\"claim\":\"University Hospital Würzburg text states the developer filed a patent during his doctoral work (Matthias Ryma) — links the IP to the university environment.\",\"url\":\"https://www.ukw.de/aktuelle-meldungen/detail/news/blutgefaesse-auf-abruf/\"}]","crowdedness":"high","competitors":"[{\"name\":\"Humacyte (now Huma)\",\"why_similar\":\"Develops acellular tissue-engineered blood vessels (off-the-shelf vascular grafts) for clinical use — same target product class (artificial/engineered vessels).\",\"funding\":\"Public company (NASDAQ-listed HUMA) with clinical-stage financing and R&D; regulatory approvals reported (Symvess approval referenced).\",\"url\":\"https://humacyte.com/acellular-tissue-engineered-vessels/\"},{\"name\":\"Vascudyne\",\"why_similar\":\"Develops engineered blood vessels intended to remodel into living tissue; preclinical and translational activity for vascular grafts.\",\"funding\":\"Company with NIH/DoD and other non-dilutive funding reported in press coverage and institutional support.\",\"url\":\"https://www.lifesciencemarketresearch.com/insights/the-memo-vascudyne-engineering-regenerative-tissue-for-cardiovascular-repair\"},{\"name\":\"Xeltis\",\"why_similar\":\"Develops bioabsorbable polymeric vascular grafts that regenerate into living tissue — clinical-stage grafts for vascular applications.\",\"funding\":\"Reported significant financing for trials (multiple funding rounds referenced in industry coverage).\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1742706125002703\"},{\"name\":\"Dialybrid\",\"why_similar\":\"Developing silk-based vascular grafts for dialysis access and other vascular applications — entered first-in-human trials.\",\"funding\":\"Raised €15M in a recent round reported in press.\",\"url\":\"https://techfundingnews.com/italian-medtech-dialybrid-raises-e15m-as-silk-based-vascular-graft-enters-first-in-human-trial/\"},{\"name\":\"VERIGRAFT\",\"why_similar\":\"Develops personalized tissue-engineered veins and vascular graft manufacturing methods — preclinical/scale-up work in vascular graft quality and production.\",\"funding\":\"Received national innovation (Vinnova) grant and collaborative funding (reported in press releases).\",\"url\":\"https://news.cision.com/se/59-north-communications/r/verigraft-to-use-ai-to-increase-quality-of-vascular-grafts%2Cc3893332\"}]","series_a_risk":"high","series_a_notes":"Businessplan Wettbewerb Nordbayern 2025 win is a positive regional validation signal based on user-provided source. Main Series A risks: university-owned IP must be exclusively licensed; crowded competitive field including Humacyte/Huma, Vascudyne, Xeltis, Dialybrid and VERIGRAFT per user input; unclear first beachhead and revenue model; biological reproducibility and manufacturing scale-up risk. Model judgement: survivability improves materially if they sell standardized preclinical vessel models/services before pursuing therapeutic grafts.","grant_bridges":"[{\"programme\":\"EXIST-Forschungstransfer\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits a university-originated, research-heavy life-science spin-out needing time to mature IP, prototype, team and transfer before VC-scale financing.\",\"source\":\"https://www.exist.de/EXIST/Navigation/DE/Gruendungsfoerderung/EXIST-Forschungstransfer/exist-forschungstransfer.html\"},{\"programme\":\"EIC Accelerator\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Potential fit if the company can evidence breakthrough innovation, European scale-up potential and a credible commercialization route for reducing animal testing in preclinical development.\",\"source\":\"https://eic.ec.europa.eu/eic-funding-opportunities/eic-accelerator_en\"},{\"programme\":\"BMBF GO-Bio initial\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Fits early life-science commercialization from academia where further validation is needed before company scale-up or larger VC rounds.\",\"source\":\"https://www.go-bio.de/gobio/de/foerderangebote/go-bio-initial/go-bio-initial_node.html\"},{\"programme\":\"BMBF Alternativmethoden zum Tierversuch\",\"why_it_fits\":\"The stated goal of reducing animal experiments aligns directly with public funding for alternative methods to animal testing.\",\"source\":\"https://www.bmbf.de/bmbf/de/forschung/gesundheit/alternativmethoden-zum-tierversuch/alternativmethoden-zum-tierversuch_node.html\"},{\"programme\":\"SPRIND funding\",\"why_it_fits\":\"Could fit only if framed as a high-impact breakthrough platform for replacing animal studies or transforming vascular testing; model judgement: less certain than EXIST/BMBF/EIC because SPRIND fit depends on a strong disruptive-use case and call/topic match.\",\"source\":\"https://www.sprind.org/en/funding/\"}]","intro_path":null,"commitment":null,"bus_factor":null,"domain_age_days":888,"deep_signals":"{\"evide